From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: t8132: Re-arm the receive wait when a
 quarantined session comes back

A quarantine wakes every waiter with complete_all(&r->received), which
leaves that completion done for good. The way back reset the open
transaction, the call deadline and the error, but not the completion. So
the first call after it, the power-up's A414, found its wait already
complete with no reply word queued. dcp_m4_runtime_next() returned
-EPROTO, which quarantined the session again with the panel dark:

  Retained DCP session quarantined: -32      (the fault injector)
  quarantined session (-32) recovered: powered down, up with the next frame
  Retained DCP session quarantined: -71
  DCP A414 failed: -71; retained session
  display power-up failed at A414: -71

Re-arm the completion while the queue is checked empty, under the state
lock that dcp_m4_runtime_receive() takes for each word and its
complete(). A powered-down DCP sends nothing meanwhile, and the
running-case power-down makes its own calls only after this.

The way back is experimental until it has passed on hardware, so
quarantine_recover now defaults to 0.

Fixes: 13c76ed4a360 ("drm: apple: t8132: Bring a quarantined display session back without a reboot")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 3f5f6e850e..10b89486c0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -338,10 +338,10 @@ module_param_cb(power_gate_ms, &power_gate_ms_ops, &power_gate_ms, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(power_gate_ms,
 		 "J713, J604: power the display coprocessor and its domains down after this many ms blanked, and before system sleep (0: only before a deep sleep; default: the machine's, J604 5000, J713/J715 0; at most 600000; applies from the next blank)");
 
-static unsigned int quarantine_recover = 1;
+static unsigned int quarantine_recover;
 module_param(quarantine_recover, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(quarantine_recover,
-		 "Internal display: bring a quarantined session back without a reboot at its next frame or system sleep (0: never; 1: only when it failed with the coprocessor powered down, the firmware untouched; 2: also try the normal power-down first when it failed running with the display off; default 1)");
+		 "Internal display: bring a quarantined session back without a reboot, from a worker after the failure and before a system sleep (0: never; 1: only when it failed with the coprocessor powered down, the firmware untouched; 2: also try the normal power-down first when it failed running with the display off; default 0; experimental)");
 
 /*
  * DCP CPU control and status, in the coprocessor's ASC block. The idle bit
@@ -6499,6 +6499,13 @@ static int __iomfb_m4_recover(struct iomfb_m4 *dcp, bool deep)
 		return -EBUSY;
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&dcp->state_lock, flags);
 	ret = r->count ? -EBUSY : 0;
+	/*
+	 * The quarantine completed the receive wait for good
+	 * (dcp_m4_runtime_wake()): with nothing queued, and nothing arriving
+	 * while it is down, it counts the queue's words again from zero.
+	 */
+	if (!ret)
+		reinit_completion(&r->received);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dcp->state_lock, flags);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-- 
